@startuml
title SIC/XE Syntax and Instruction Format Resolution
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #455A64
  ArrowColor #546E7A
}

[*] --> Source

state "Source line" as Source
state "Lexical helpers\n\nStrip comments outside quotes\nscan whitespace-delimited fields\nsplit operands on commas outside literals" as Lex
state "Resolve first field\n\nKnown instruction/directive -> operation\notherwise -> label, then read operation\nuppercase name for lookup" as FirstField
state "ISA / directive lookup\n\nInstructionDef: opcode, base format,\nOperandSchema, SIC support\nDirectiveKind resolved separately" as Lookup
state "Operand alias check\n\nRegister-first ADD/SUB/MUL/DIV/COMP\nselect ADDR/SUBR/MULR/DIVR/COMPR\nTIX + register selects TIXR" as Alias
state "Parse by schema\n\nMemory: expr, optional # / @, optional $X\nReg / RegReg / RegCount / Number\nvalidate arity and register names" as Schema
state "Select architecture and size" as Size
state "SIC mode\n\n3-byte instruction size\nreject unsupported instruction, '+',\nand immediate / indirect mode" as SIC
state "SIC/XE mode\n\nFormat 1 -> 1 byte\nFormat 2 -> 2 bytes\nFormat 3 -> 3 bytes\n'+' -> format 4 (4 bytes) only when\nInstructionDef allows extension" as XE
state "Format-3 address selection\n\nForced ,p or ,b -> validate that mode\nAutomatic -> PC-relative if in range;\nelse BASE-relative if active and in range;\nelse direct 12-bit if absolute and in range;\notherwise error suggests '+'\nNo automatic format-4 promotion" as AddressMode
state "Directive path\n\nDirectiveKind-specific parsing and validation\nPass 1 handles layout and symbols\nPass 2 emits BYTE / WORD data where needed" as DirectivePath
state "Encode bytes" as Encode
state "Diagnostics + AssemblyResult" as Result

Source --> Lex
Lex --> FirstField
FirstField --> Lookup : operation
Lookup --> Alias : instruction
Lookup --> DirectivePath : directive
Lookup --> Result : unknown operation
Alias --> Schema
Schema --> Size
Size --> SIC : SIC option
Size --> XE : SIC/XE option
SIC --> Encode
XE --> AddressMode : format-3 memory
XE --> Encode : format 1 / 2 / 4 or non-memory
AddressMode --> Encode
Encode --> Result
DirectivePath --> Result
Result --> [*]

note right of Lookup
The language server sends this vocabulary to Monaco's
Monarch tokenizer during initialize for token coloring.
Coloring is separate from parser validation and format selection.
end note

note bottom of AddressMode
Out-of-range format-3 targets are diagnosed.
The user must explicitly add '+' for format 4.
end note
@enduml
